                <pb facs="0865" n="729" sameAs="frus:frus1929v01/pg729"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">723.2515/3269: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Peru</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Moore</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Lima</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-02-27T20:00:00-05:00">February 27, 1929—8
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 9:18 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>22. Your 16, February 27, noon. President Leguia will probably discuss cost of
                    new port when he delivers engineers’ report to Ambassador Figueroa. I will
                    telegraph immediately when President Leguia submits it.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Moore</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
